Error [jet.UninferableTypeArgument]: `Slot` is generic, so `Slot.reflect()` has no payload types to list its cases with
  --> tests/ui/enum_cases_refuse_generic_without_arguments.jet:9:21
    |
  9 |     info: #run Slot.reflect()
    |                     ^^^^^^^
 Why: A case catalog describes each payload at one type, and a generic enum named without its type arguments is a family of types
 Fix: Name one type per parameter, as `Slot<…>.reflect()`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0904
